## 14. Longest Common Prefix

## Approach
--  Take the first string as the reference string.
--  Traverse each character of the reference string using index i.
--  For every i, compare that character with the same index in every other string.
--  If any string is shorter or the characters don't match, stop the comparison.
--  If all strings match at that index, increase the prefixLength.
--  Finally, return the first prefixLength characters from the reference string.

## Complexity :
Time: O(n × m)
Space: O(1)

where n = number of strings and m = length of the shortest string.

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public String longestCommonPrefix(String[] strs) {
        String reference = strs[0];
        int prefixLength = 0;
        boolean mismatch = false;
        for (int i = 0; i < reference.length(); i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < strs.length; j++) {
                if (i >= strs[j].length()) { // at any portion i is greater than the next string index i which means the first reference string ends
                    mismatch = true;
                    break;
                } else if (reference.charAt(i) != strs[j].charAt(i)) {
                    mismatch = true;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (mismatch)
                break;
            prefixLength++;
        }
        return reference.substring(0, prefixLength); // it returns all character which matches in all strings from starting with the first string as a reference
    }
}
